* CABSRT14 - MEDIA EXTRACT SORT FOR THE TAPE DESPATCH
* THE TAPE IS WRITTEN IN CARRIER ORDER SO THAT ONE VOLUME CAN BE
* SPLIT BETWEEN CARRIERS AT THE BUREAU.  THE LABEL AND TRAILER
* RECORDS MUST STAY AT THE FRONT AND BACK, WHICH IS WHAT THE
* LEADING SORT KEY ON THE TYPE BYTE DOES.
*
* THE OUTFIL BELOW DROPS EVERY DETAIL RECORD WHOSE AMOUNT IS
* ZERO.  THE TRAILER HASH WRITTEN BY CABFMT07 STILL INCLUDES
* THEM, SO THE BUREAU RECONCILIATION HAS NEVER TIED EXACTLY AND
* THE TOLERANCE THEY APPLY WAS AGREED IN 1997.
 SORT FIELDS=(1,1,CH,A,15,14,CH,A,29,6,CH,A)
 OUTFIL OMIT=(1,1,CH,EQ,C'D',AND,375,8,PD,EQ,0)
 OPTION EQUALS
 RECORD TYPE=F,LENGTH=400
